<title>NORWAY: Norway buys armaments from Bofors.</title>
<headline>Norway buys armaments from Bofors.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Norwegian Defence Ministry approved on Thursday a 228 million crown contract with Swedish defence contractor Bofors AB.</p>
<p>The state procurement office will buy night-vision sights for the Robot 70 surface-to-air missile system from Bofors, a statement said.</p>
<p>Bofors and sub-contractor CelsiusTech Electronics, in return, committed themselves to allocate some of the production to Norway's Narvik Technology AS.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
